{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774127573,"nonce":"qFn59i6EWh3YowZwdcRLzFo1mro=","title":"Generalize auth queue: authenticated action types beyond merges","message":"The auth queue currently only handles merge requests (protected branch merges via mandible auth request). It should generalize to \"authenticated action requests\" with a type field.\n\nAction types to support:\n1. merge — current behavior (protected branch merge with YubiKey signing)\n2. commit — direct commit to protected branch (agent-commit currently bypasses auth)\n3. force-push — git push --force\n4. branch-delete — deletion of protected/important branches\n5. config-change — security-relevant settings changes (protected branch designation, hook disabling)\n6. preset-promote — promoting a convention to global CLAUDE.md\n7. data-delete — clearing conversation history, deleting presets, purging caches\n\nThe auth_requests table would need a `type` column (default: \"merge\" for backward compat). The UI already has approval/rejection flow — it needs type-specific rendering (different icons, descriptions, actions per type).\n\nThis is a pre-release architectural change that enables proper access control as Mandible grows.","files":null}]}